{# The two asset links every generated page carries — LOCAL FIRST, CDN if the
   local copy is absent. NOT a component: named _assets.html.j2, so
   load_components() never registers it. Included by reports/report.master.html.j2 and
   components/_showcase.html.j2, so the strategy is defined once and a report
   and a showcase can never disagree about it.

   `local_href` is the relative path from WHERE THE FILE IS WRITTEN back to this
   skill (builder.local_href) — a showcase three folders deep gets `../../..`, a
   report in docs/ gets whatever reaches the skill from there. It is empty when
   no relative path exists (a different drive), and then only the CDN is linked.

   WHY BOTH. Local first, so a page previews the CURRENT tree the moment it is
   generated — no publish, no cache, no version bump between editing a
   stylesheet and seeing it. CDN second, so the same file still renders once it
   leaves the tree: copied elsewhere, emailed, opened from a download folder.
   The fallback is what makes a generated page portable AND live.

   HOW THE FALLBACK FIRES. `onerror` on the tag itself — the browser tells us
   the local file is missing, so nothing has to poll or guess, and a page whose
   local assets are present pays nothing. The stylesheet retargets the SAME
   element (a link re-fetches when its href changes). The script cannot: a
   <script> that failed will not re-fetch on a new src, so the handler appends a
   fresh element. That late script still initialises the page — js/modules/main.js
   checks `document.readyState` and calls init() directly when the DOM is already
   parsed, which is exactly this case. #}
{% if local_href %}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ local_href }}/css/bundle.css"
        onerror="this.onerror=null;this.href='{{ cdn_href }}/css/bundle.css'">
  <script src="{{ local_href }}/js/bundle.js" defer
          onerror="var s=document.createElement('script');s.src='{{ cdn_href }}/js/bundle.js';document.head.appendChild(s)"></script>
{% else %}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ cdn_href }}/css/bundle.css">
  <script src="{{ cdn_href }}/js/bundle.js" defer></script>
{% endif %}
